Paint the rich panel body, and bound it correctly.

Three bugs from the rich row path, all invisible until it ran against a live
compositor.

The panel was transparent everywhere except the search row and the selection
pill. The classic row loop never needed a body fill: bm_cairo_draw_line paints
a background box behind every text run, so the panel came out opaque as a side
effect of drawing text. Rich rows only fill the selection pill, and the surface
is cleared to nothing at the top of bm_cairo_paint, so everything else showed
whatever was behind the layer surface.

The reported height was the last drawn row's bottom rather than the panel's.
With BM_ALIGN_CENTER the surface is anchored to both the top and bottom edges,
so an under-reported height does not merely crop the panel, it moves it: the
compositor centres the size it was given.

Rows were laid out until the bottom of the screen rather than the bottom of the
panel. The rounded clip hid the overrun, but only after a row had been
positioned and counted, leaving a sliver of a tenth row under a nine-row panel
and a displayed count that disagreed with what was visible.

total_height also now accounts for the taller search row and for line_height
being the list row height in rich mode, rather than reusing the single shared
text height.

Rebased on patch 02's pill_count-gated heading condition (`if (menu->
pill_count == 0 && section && *section && ...)`): the list_bottom rename this
patch makes to that same line's max_height check now lands on 02's already-
gated form, carried forward here as unchanged context. total_height and
list_bottom stay exactly the math described above regardless of whether
headings are being drawn: list_bottom bounds `lines * row_h` of vertical
space for item rows the same way with or without a pill bar, and headings
were always additional consumption inside that budget rather than added to
it, so pill mode drawing zero of them simply lets more of the existing budget
go to item rows — no formula here needed to change for that, only the two
touched lines' text to line up with 02's rewritten condition.

